cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Neural Surrogates for Path-Dependent Volatility: Fast Online Assimilation of Streaming Option Quotes with Guardrails"
authors:
  - family-names: "Trestka"
    given-names: "Konrad"
    affiliation: "University of Minnesota"
repository-code: "https://github.com/KonradT22/VolatilityIsMostlyPathDependent"
abstract: >
  An inverse neural surrogate for calibrating a non-Markovian Path-Dependent Volatility
  model from option surfaces, with statistical (Mahalanobis / Ledoit-Wolf) and numerical
  guardrails for unsupported market states. University of Minnesota UROP research project,
  advised by Prof. John Dodson. Builds on the 4-factor Markovian PDV Monte Carlo
  implementation from Guyon & Lekeufack, "Volatility Is (Mostly) Path-Dependent."
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Volatility Is (Mostly) Path-Dependent"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Guyon"
        given-names: "Julien"
      - family-names: "Lekeufack"
        given-names: "Jordan"
